    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Dealing with physical gold or silver must have been a massive security headache. Given the risks of banditry and the isolation of these routes, were there any specific cultural groups or merchant networks that became particularly dominant in managing these complex financial transactions? I'm looking for more of the human element of how this trust was actually built.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
